<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gold Fields Namibia Q2 net loss 9.67m rand.</title>
<headline>Gold Fields Namibia Q2 net loss 9.67m rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss before capital spending    9.67 vs 15.63 profit</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  0.81 vs 2.99</p>
<p>Metal in concentrates produced:</p>
<p>    - copper (tonnes)			4,120 vs 2,948</p>
<p>    - lead (tonnes)			  1,069 vs 917</p>
<p>    - silver (tonnes)			   10 vs 8</p>
<p>Metal produced from smelters:</p>
<p>    - copper in blister (tonnes)	 5,088 vs 5,605</p>
<p>    - refined lead (tonnes)		  686 vs -</p>
<p>Metal sold:</p>
<p>    - copper (tonnes)			5,342 vs 4,557</p>
<p>    - lead (tonnes)			    338 vs 120</p>
<p>    - silver (tonnes)			   11 vs 10</p>
<p>    Ore milled (tonnes)		  512,000 vs 248,000</p>
<p>    Sales					69.40 vs 55,034</p>
<p>    Cost of sales			    79.51 vs 72,778</p>
<p>Full name: Gold Fields Namibia Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - no dividend was declared.</p>
<p>- The company said its new Ausmelt lead smelter had not</p>
<p>fully overcome the operational problems which arose from the extended period between bricking the furnace and hot commissioning.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
